{
	title: 'A notify tool posts a notice mid-turn',
	spec: 'A notify tool with exactly one text argument (one non-empty line under 80 Unicode characters; no control characters) posts an attention notice from the running turn, for example when the user asked to be told if an approach fails. It routes through the same delivery path as any notice (task qm): nothing if the session is watched, a notice carrying the text to clients watching another tab with no push, else a push carrying the text. It answers sent. Cancelled or invalid calls deliver nothing. A tool, not a tag: mid-turn the turn goes on anyway, so it costs no extra request beyond the ordinary tool-result continuation and is structured. Notifications are side effects, not read-only tools.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'notify.deliver is shared by automatic notice routing and the notify tool; the tool does not broadcast a fake question or turn-end event, or interrupt the turn.'
	],
	needs: ['x8']
}
